= Primacy effect =

== Overview ==
The '''primacy effect''' is an advantage for information encountered early in a sequence.

== Human cognition ==
In memory experiments, early list items can receive more rehearsal or become more distinct from later interference. Primacy effects also occur in impression formation, judgment, and choice.

== Distinguish the phenomenon from mechanism ==
“Primacy” names a positional pattern. It does not by itself identify why early information received greater weight.

== Language models ==
LLM evaluations have reported primacy effects caused by answer-option order and prompt position. These should be measured by controlled order permutations rather than inferred from a single response.

== References ==
* Solomon E. Asch, “Forming Impressions of Personality”, ''Journal of Abnormal and Social Psychology'' 41 (1946): 258–290.
* Bennet B. Murdock Jr. (1962), serial-position research.
* Itzhak et al., “Instructed to Bias: Instruction-Tuned Language Models Exhibit Emergent Cognitive Bias”, EMNLP 2023.

